      <description>&lt;!-- Pick your favourite water/wastewater innovation (technological, institutional, regulatory, etc) and investigate and analyse a scenario each where it has been implemented: 1) successfully, and 2) unsuccessfully. 

A) What are the key takeaways from your investigation? (Hint: Think about the best way to convey your findings to a general audience)

B) How could your findings on your innovation be applied to the Perth/Western Australian context?

Take into account all of the material we have covered thus far in the unit, and don&#39;t forget the SDGs! --&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;A history of Perth&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perth&amp;rsquo;s history has been marked by water scarcity issues from its earlier colonisation. Water restrictions have been periodically implemented to reduce water use through summer conditions &lt;a href=&#34;https://miwer.org/2019/12/history-of-water-use-in-the-perth-bunbury-region-2/&#34;&gt;for over 100 years&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Industry, Innovation, Infrastructure</title>
